WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:02.519
Line 3 makes numbers.

2
00:00:03.233 --> 00:00:08.272
Data and digital manufacturing teaches you to turn those numbers into decisions.

3
00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:13.466
The unit’s numbers go to the MES and to a screen by the line.

4
00:00:14.442 --> 00:00:15.615
You are the engineer.

5
00:00:16.442 --> 00:00:20.656
You start with the numbers themselves, with data quality and dashboards.

6
00:00:21.737 --> 00:00:26.381
Then comes what carries them further, with integration and with AI and models.

7
00:00:27.689 --> 00:00:29.756
The first topic is Data quality.

8
00:00:30.444 --> 00:00:32.963
Good data are fit for the use you have in mind.

9
00:00:34.004 --> 00:00:37.626
The unit’s numbers have to be on time and they have to be right.

10
00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:42.026
You read them from the PLC cabinet with an edge gateway.

11
00:00:43.305 --> 00:00:46.614
The second topic is Dashboards and visual management.

12
00:00:47.413 --> 00:00:50.327
A KPI shows whether you are on track for a goal.

13
00:00:51.305 --> 00:00:54.382
You want to see that number by the line at a glance.

14
00:00:55.365 --> 00:00:57.815
For that you follow the line on a dashboard.

15
00:00:59.162 --> 00:01:01.124
The third topic is Integration.

16
00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:06.667
Every number is born somewhere, such as in the PLC or in the MES.

17
00:01:07.675 --> 00:01:11.251
A data platform brings those sources together for reports.

18
00:01:12.257 --> 00:01:14.718
You store the numbers in a data warehouse.

19
00:01:16.012 --> 00:01:18.566
The fourth topic is AI and models.

20
00:01:19.265 --> 00:01:21.854
A model learns a pattern from examples.

21
00:01:22.869 --> 00:01:25.493
A model is only as good as its data.

22
00:01:26.208 --> 00:01:28.727
You often have few examples of failures.

23
00:01:29.759 --> 00:01:32.696
You let anomaly detection flag what deviates.

24
00:01:33.415 --> 00:01:35.737
A deviation is not always broken.

25
00:01:36.741 --> 00:01:39.876
That is how the numbers of line 3 become decisions.

26
00:01:41.163 --> 00:01:41.918
The whole map.

27
00:01:42.661 --> 00:01:48.327
Data and digital manufacturing is the fifth and last station of Automation and IT.

28
00:01:49.316 --> 00:01:51.499
Each of the four topics has four levels.

29
00:01:52.521 --> 00:01:56.422
Start at Basics level with the six dimensions of data quality.

30
00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:58.835
They give words for what is wrong.

31
00:01:59.857 --> 00:02:04.710
At Working knowledge level come machine data, Power BI, from source to report.

32
00:02:05.479 --> 00:02:07.244
Also predictive maintenance.

33
00:02:08.257 --> 00:02:12.646
At Advanced level come master data and MES, the floor screen,

34
00:02:12.867 --> 00:02:14.643
ownership and AI inspection.

35
00:02:15.662 --> 00:02:18.390
At Expert level come managing data quality,

36
00:02:18.588 --> 00:02:21.885
alert fatigue, the business case and digital twins.

37
00:02:22.907 --> 00:02:27.052
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
